{
  "name": "The directive names the earliest unmet prerequisite of an in-window routine step",
  "why": "A routine step's window is fixed in advance and is not recomputed when the person runs late, so a prerequisite can fall out of its window while the step that depends on it comes into window. Directing the dependent step would name something the start gate refuses, because every prerequisite must be completed first. The directive must walk the dependencies from the in-window step to the earliest unmet prerequisite (\"Prepare clothes\") and direct that, and the projected day starts with the same pending steps in order ahead of the commitment. Note: no mutant bites this case (skipping the prerequisite walk changes nothing here), so it pins today's behaviour only.",
